    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "These documents give the rule the twentieth century inherited and show it applied: Mexico under Porfirio Díaz (1877–78), Ecuador (1895), Venezuela (1899), Colombia (1900) and Nicaragua (1911), plus a general statement of the three conditions written in 1913. The thread is what the Department wrote down as the test, and what it asked a new regime to do beyond meeting it."
